      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 9.82,
          "en": "With the meetup grid added, It's now also time to make sure that we can add meetups now for adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 9.82,
          "end": 10.27,
          "en": "meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.27,
          "end": 12.7,
          "en": "I'll start in the app Svelte file later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.7,
          "end": 17.89,
          "en": "We'll outsource this functionality into a different component too, but for the moment we would hit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.89,
          "end": 22.96,
          "en": "a problem when we want to pass data around and I'll show which problem this is later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.96,
          "end": 29.26,
          "en": "For now, let's just add our, um, our add form, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 30.01,
          "end": 36.34,
          "en": "So in here I'll add a form element with no action because I don't want to send an Http request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 36.34,
          "end": 37.75,
          "en": "in the main section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 37.75,
          "end": 42.28,
          "en": "This is our form and in there we need a couple of inputs and we need a button now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 42.28,
          "end": 45.19,
          "en": "We need inputs for all the data fields we have in a meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 45.19,
          "end": 48.97,
          "en": "We have a title, subtitle description, image, URL, address and contact email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 49,
          "end": 51.4,
          "en": "The ID will be generated automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 52.24,
          "end": 55.63,
          "en": "Therefore, in here, let's maybe add a couple of divs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 55.66,
          "end": 60.7,
          "en": "Each div receives a class of form control just for styling reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.7,
          "end": 66.52,
          "en": "Then we have a label, um, for the title for example, where we say title and below that we have a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.52,
          "end": 69.91,
          "en": "input of type text with ID title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 78.12,
          "en": "Now we can repeat this a couple of times for the different pieces of data we're collecting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 78.12,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "So we have the subtitle here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 82.86,
          "en": "So here we also want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "Use the subtitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "We also have our.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 90.88,
          "end": 91.42,
          "en": "Um.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 91.42,
          "end": 92.62,
          "en": "Address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 94.12,
          "end": 95.56,
          "en": "Which we handle like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 95.65,
          "end": 99.82,
          "en": "We have our image URL which should be entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 100.58,
          "end": 101.74000000000001,
          "en": "Image URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 102.39,
          "end": 103.44,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 106.27000000000001,
          "en": "We also what else do we have?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "We also have a description and our contact email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.94,
          "end": 113.84,
          "en": "So let's continue with the email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 113.85,
          "end": 119.22,
          "en": "This will be for email and the type here will also be email on mobile devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.22,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "This ensures that we get the right keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "And last but not least, we'll have another form control for the description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 131.7,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "But here, this is not an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 134.04,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "This will actually be a text area and this is not a self-closing tag, but we need to close it like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 140.43,
          "en": "this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 140.43,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "And it has no type, but it has rows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "And actually you can write that as a self-closing tab here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "That would not be a regular HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "But since this is parsed by Svelte first, it gives you some extra shortcuts where it automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "extends this to the right HTML markup once this gets shipped to the browser, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 164.19,
          "end": 165.48,
          "en": "So this is our form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "Super ugly, obviously, but it has the fields we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 168.3,
          "end": 170.37,
          "en": "Let's also add a button in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 171.46,
          "end": 171.91,
          "en": "Um.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 173.42000000000002,
          "en": "In here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.44,
          "end": 178.8,
          "en": "The button where we say save button type will be submit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 180.96,
          "en": "And now we could add a click listener here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 180.96,
          "end": 186.39,
          "en": "But actually, when we have a submit button in a form, what will happen is that the form gets submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 186.39,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "So here we can listen to on submit on the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 193.35,
          "en": "We haven't done that before in the course and on click on the button would also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.35,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "But this approach here is even a bit more correct, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 200.34,
          "en": "So we have on submit and important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "I want to prevent the default here so that no Http request gets sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 209.1,
          "en": "Instead, we can handle this entirely on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 209.31,
          "end": 212.16,
          "en": "So we got on submit like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 212.28,
          "end": 219.36,
          "en": "Now when we do click submit here, I want to trigger a function which we have to add in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 219.36,
          "end": 221.22,
          "en": "here in our script section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 228.99,
          "en": "Add meetup like this, and I'm simply pointing at this function here between curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 228.99,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "These are always required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 234.55,
          "en": "And now here, this does not output data because it's on an event handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 234.57999999999998,
          "end": 240.61,
          "en": "Therefore here this always should be a pointer at a function which gets executed when this event gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 240.61,
          "end": 241.24,
          "en": "triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 242.53,
          "end": 244.96,
          "en": "So with that, we have this function place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 244.96,
          "end": 250.75,
          "en": "We have this ugly form in place Before we take care about the styling, let's actually add the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 250.75,
          "end": 251.88,
          "en": "for adding a meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 251.89,
          "end": 255.76,
          "en": "So at meetup runs when we submit this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 255.76,
          "end": 262.3,
          "en": "Now of course, to fetch all these inputs, we have to store the values the user enters and for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 262.3,
          "end": 265.15,
          "en": "we can use the two way binding syntax you learn about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 266.05,
          "end": 268.75,
          "en": "You can add a couple of variables here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 269.48,
          "end": 273.32,
          "en": "Title and so on, and I'll initialize them with empty strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 273.32,
          "end": 281.42,
          "en": "So we have the same for subtitle, we have the same for the address with the same for the email and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 281.42,
          "end": 281.96,
          "en": "so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 281.96,
          "end": 288.05,
          "en": "So let's just initialize all the variables that hold the data we expect the user to enter and now we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 288.05,
          "end": 289.34000000000003,
          "en": "can bind this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 289.37,
          "end": 289.7,
          "en": "Oops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 289.7,
          "end": 293.96,
          "en": "We also need the image URL and now we can bind this to our inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 294.68,
          "end": 297.2,
          "en": "With that special bind directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 297.73,
          "end": 304.15,
          "en": "So here on the title input, for example, we can use bind value and set this equal to title and title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 304.15,
          "end": 307.42,
          "en": "here simply refers to this title variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 307.42,
          "end": 312.55,
          "en": "So we set the value that's stored in here initially an empty string as a value for the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 312.55,
          "end": 317.14,
          "en": "But once we type there, the entered value will be saved back into this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 317.14,
          "end": 321.04,
          "en": "So this is a live connection we set up with the help of the Bind directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 322.21,
          "end": 324.67,
          "en": "Now I will use the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 325.34,
          "end": 326.9,
          "en": "For the subtitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 326.9,
          "end": 333.62,
          "en": "So let's exchange title for subtitle here and repeat the same for address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 333.8,
          "end": 336.68,
          "en": "For image URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 337.68,
          "end": 340.23,
          "en": "For email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 341.55,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "And of course also for description, which I also created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 346.32,
          "en": "Yes, I did so for description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 346.32,
          "end": 351.36,
          "en": "And here also on the text area, you add bind value description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 351.57,
          "end": 353.52,
          "en": "With that, all the data is stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 353.52,
          "end": 360.12,
          "en": "Now in Add Meetup, we want to add our meetup to the meetups array so we can create a new meetup here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 360.12,
          "end": 361.92,
          "en": "which is a new JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 361.92,
          "end": 365.25,
          "en": "And now that should have the same structure as our other meetups here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 365.25,
          "end": 372.3,
          "en": "So we need an ID and for now I will generate that with Math.random, which again is not truly unique,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 372.3,
          "end": 373.56,
          "en": "but fair enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 373.56,
          "end": 375.21,
          "en": "And I'll convert it to a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 375.21,
          "end": 381.33,
          "en": "You don't have to do that, but I'm using string IDs here too, so I want to continue using that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 381.33,
          "end": 387.45,
          "en": "And then I add a title property to that object and the value will be the value stored in that title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 387.45,
          "end": 390.69,
          "en": "variable because that is the variable bound to our inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 390.69,
          "end": 398.97,
          "en": "So here we can now set title and I do the same for subtitle, of course, the same for description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 398.97,
          "end": 402.76,
          "en": "the same for the image URL and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 403.24,
          "end": 407.08,
          "en": "Important for the email, I named it contact email for the other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 407.38,
          "end": 407.72,
          "en": "Um.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 409.21,
          "end": 413.38,
          "en": "Meet up here, so we should use contact email here to the variable that stores.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 413.38,
          "end": 415.33,
          "en": "The email though, is just named email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 415.33,
          "end": 416.83,
          "en": "So here this differs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 416.83,
          "end": 421.6,
          "en": "We have email on the right referring to that variable and contact email on the left, referring to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 421.6,
          "end": 425.08,
          "en": "property that should be added to our meetup object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 425.17,
          "end": 427.72,
          "en": "We also have our address of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 428.97,
          "end": 430.32,
          "en": "So that is a new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 430.32,
          "end": 436.35,
          "en": "Now, that new meetup here, of course, should be added to the meetups and you'll learn that this does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 436.35,
          "end": 437.22,
          "en": "not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 437.25,
          "end": 439.26,
          "en": "Meetups Push new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 439.38,
          "end": 443.76,
          "en": "Now it's important that you know that, but it's also important that you know why it doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 443.76,
          "end": 445.53,
          "en": "So do you know why it doesn't work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 446.25,
          "end": 453.57,
          "en": "The problem here was that this is not a trigger that signals to svelte that it needs to check the Dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 453.57,
          "end": 455.64,
          "en": "and potentially update the dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 455.67,
          "end": 458.13,
          "en": "The trigger is the equal sign instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 458.13,
          "end": 460.95,
          "en": "So this here is simply not picked up by svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 460.98,
          "end": 464.58,
          "en": "So this does not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 465.6,
          "end": 471.18,
          "en": "Instead, what you should do is set meetups equal to a new array created here with square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 471.18,
          "end": 477.33,
          "en": "and then we can use some modern JavaScript syntax, take all our old meetups with the spread operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 477.33,
          "end": 479.5,
          "en": "and then add the new meetup like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 479.52,
          "end": 484.83,
          "en": "Or if you want to add the new meetup in front, which I do, you simply add it as the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
